```json
[
 {
  "id": "F1",
  "file": "src/land/deploy-process.ts",
  "line": 124,
  "title": "The plaintext credentials file is readable by agents",
  "detail": "deployProcess writes every registered credential to ~/.limitless/logs/<label>.credentials. File modes don't stop processes running as the same user, and that directory isn't in the read-deny list that tool-enabled editors and readers get (src/harness/read-policy.ts; src/harness/codex.ts), so an agent running concurrently can read all factory secrets while the file exists. The file also survives some paths: death before submit returns, a filter that fails before unlinking, and the wrapper's relaunch branch, which never removes it. Put the file only where every confined process (gate, Claude editor/reader, Codex) is already denied reads, for example beside the other private credentials, or add its exact location to the shared deny list. Remove it on every path, including the relaunch branch and the boot reconcile. Prove it with a real Seatbelt probe (test.skipIf(seatbeltSkip !== null), title including seatbeltSkip, per AGENTS.md): a confined reader can't read the file while the deploy runs, and a control read of an allowed path succeeds."
 },
 {
  "id": "F2",
  "file": "src/land/deploy-process.ts",
  "line": 201,
  "title": "Cleanup treats a failed launchctl inspection as the job being gone",
  "detail": "removeDeployJob (and deployJobStatus's missing-job path) treat any nonzero result of `launchctl list <label>` as absence. With allowFail a timeout returns exitCode null, so a slow launchctl makes cleanup delete the status and started marker and report success; AutoDeploy then drops the durable job id while the job may still be registered, and without the started marker a relaunch deploys again. Treat only launchctl's definite not-found result as absence; on any other failure keep the job id and markers and retry on the next tick. Add tests for a timed-out list during removal and during status checks."
 },
 {
  "id": "F3",
  "file": "src/land/redact-deploy.ts",
  "line": 7,
  "title": "A failing redaction filter can kill the deploy mid-way, or go unnoticed",
  "detail": "The deploy writes into the filter's pipe. If the filter throws before it starts reading stdin (missing or invalid credentials file, unlink failure), the pipe closes and the deploy's next write gets EPIPE/SIGPIPE; `limitless deploy` can then die between checking out the candidate and restarting, or during health checks, bypassing its rollback. Make the filter unable to stop reading early: on any setup error, keep draining stdin to EOF and write only a fixed `[deploy output withheld: redaction unavailable]` line (never unredacted text). Record the filter's own exit status as well and include `log unavailable` in the recorded outcome when it failed, without changing the deploy's exit status. Add a test where the filter's credentials file is invalid: the deploy command still completes and its status is recorded."
 }
]
